## Maintenance Commands

This rule documents how `/cleanup` and `/back` must behave.

### Principles

- Do not remove or alter existing features or UI
- Favor minimal, focused edits; keep diffs small
- Enforce i18n rules: any removed keys must be removed symmetrically from both `en` and `de`
- Create a safety snapshot (branch + tag) before destructive changes
- Prefer preview → confirmation → apply

### Cleanup Scope

- `www` → `apps/www`
- `api` → `apps/api`
- no arg → repository root

### Allowed Deletions

- Unused translation keys (verified by code references)
- Orphaned components/assets not imported anywhere
- Unreferenced CSS utilities/variables
- Demo/story files clearly not part of shipped UI

### Not Allowed

- Removing exported components used directly or indirectly by pages
- Removing keys referenced by `t(...)`, `useTranslations(...)`, or server variants
- Changing visible text outside i18n files

### Rollback

- `/back` restores to the most recent safety snapshot created by the maintenance commands

